  Two toolchain limits — worked around, not papered over

  pySHACL can't do the empty-I check. It flattens the dataset before validating,
  so GRAPH inside sh:sparql raises "requiring a dataset… but operating 
  currently on a single graph" — I tested Graph, ConjunctiveGraph and Dataset,
  all identical, so it isn't a loading problem. Rather than ship a shape that
  silently never fires, it's empty_interface.rq. That uses FILTER NOT EXISTS
  because rdflib also raises NotBoundError inside COUNT/GROUP_CONCAT/SAMPLE when
  the aggregated variable is unbound — precisely the case being looked for.

