  The editorial note ("may be normalized... to something other than escaped
  values") specifies nothing, and collides with the encoding RFC 6570 already
  defines. Delete it; specify Level 1 exactly. Slugging (Longitudinal Load →
  longitudinal_load) is a real want, but it's a separate opt-in with its own
  vocabulary, and it isn't needed to make minting work.

  6. Termination

  CONCAT, ENCODE_FOR_URI and IRI are pure, so a minted IRI is a deterministic
  function of L-bound values. Re-running mints the same IRI, prune_known! sees
  nothing new, and the fixpoint converges normally. Determinism is what makes 
  minting safe — it isn't a restriction imposed for caution.

