  Rewrite mode

  The interesting result: triple-level I is set arithmetic, not a research 
  problem. Because variables are persistent individuals rather than
  name-strings, two pattern triples denote the same thing exactly when they're
  the same RDF triple.

  Reversibility needed the real design work. DROP GRAPH undoes an addition and
  can do nothing about a deletion, so the removed triples go to a tombstone in
  the same atomic update that removes them. Measured: 5 triples → 3, undo
  restores all 5 exactly.

  Constraints I chose deliberately: exactly one target graph ("delete from the
  union of these three" is neither expressible nor reviewable), applies once
  (iterating a deleting rule needs NACs), and confirm = true required over MCP
  with explain_rule leading on removals.

